Zainium OS
==========

Zainium OS is an independent Linux operating system by Zainium Dynamics. It is
not based on any other distribution. It uses the Linux kernel (linux-evl), the
musl C library, systemd as init, and the COSMIC desktop. It runs on x86_64 and
is licensed under GPL-3.0.

Zainium OS takes a different approach from other Linux distributions. The main
differences are below.


1. No /usr, /etc, /bin or /lib at the root
------------------------------------------

The root directory holds only the virtual file systems (/dev, /proc, /sys,
/run, /tmp), /home, /root, and /overlayer. The whole operating system lives
under /overlayer:

  /overlayer/syshub    the base system (programs, libraries, configuration)
  /overlayer/zexlib    software you install, and the package records
  /overlayer/zaisys    the kernel, the initramfs and the boot loader files
  /overlayer/agents    instructions and skills for AI coding agents

Programs are built for these paths. For programs that still look for /usr,
/etc or /bin, the libsys_resolver library maps those paths to the Zainium
ones, if the requested path does not exist. It only works for dynamically
linked programs that are not setuid.


2. The base and your software are separate layers
-------------------------------------------------

The base system (syshub) and the software you install (zexlib/union) are kept
in different places on disk. At boot, quantra-ramfs (the initramfs) joins them
with OverlayFS into one view at /overlayer/syshub. Programs see a single
system. On disk, nothing you install is written into the base.

The base is not changed while the system runs. Base upgrades are downloaded
and staged, then applied at the next boot, before the system is mounted. The
last applied upgrade can be undone at the next boot. Your installed software
can be removed or wiped without touching the base.

As root, `elevate` refuses commands such as rm, mv and cp on the base, the
boot files and a staged upgrade.


3. musl in the base, glibc in its own directory
-----------------------------------------------

The base is built from source against musl with the x86_64-zainium-linux-musl
toolchain. musl and its loader live in their own directory:

  /overlayer/syshub/x86_64-zainium-linux-musl/lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1

There is no glibc in the base, and base upgrades reject glibc-linked files.

glibc is a package with its own directory, apart from musl's:

  elevate zex install glibc             loader, libraries, locales, tools
  elevate zex install glibc-toolchain   gcc and g++ for glibc, with glibc-dev

  /overlayer/zexlib/union/x86_64-zainium-linux-gnu/lib/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2

Nothing of glibc goes into the shared bin, lib or include directories, so gcc,
ldd, the headers and every musl program stay musl's. A glibc program runs with
glibc's loader and loads libraries only from glibc's directory: the libraries
of the base are built for musl and cannot load into it. glibc reads the
system's configuration in /overlayer/syshub/etc (users, hosts, DNS, timezone).
A program built elsewhere that asks for /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 is started
with glibc's loader. To build for glibc, use x86_64-zainium-linux-gnu-gcc or
x86_64-zainium-linux-gnu-g++; plain gcc builds for musl.


4. One package manager: zex
---------------------------

zex installs native Zainium packages (.zex) first. When Zainium's archive does
not have a package, zex can install it from Void Linux (musl), Alpine Linux or
Chimera Linux, and adjusts it to the Zainium paths (program loader, library
search path, script interpreters). Before installing, zex checks that every
library the package needs is available, and it never replaces a file of the
base. See /overlayer/zex.md.

Desktop applications are also available through Flatpak (zex install flatpak)
and the COSMIC Store.


Main components
---------------

  Boot loader      Limine (UEFI and BIOS)
  Kernel           linux-evl
  Initramfs        quantra-ramfs (finds the disk, joins the layers, applies
                   staged base upgrades, starts the Plymouth splash)
  Init             systemd
  Login            greetd with cosmic-greeter
  Desktop          COSMIC
  Packages         zex
  Root access      elevate (replaces sudo), elevate-pam
  Network, audio   NetworkManager, PipeWire


Status
------

Zainium OS is in active development.

- Not every package from Void, Alpine or Chimera works after adjustment. zex
  refuses packages whose libraries no repository provides, unless you confirm.
- Programs that hard-code /usr, /etc or /bin paths and are static or setuid
  are not covered by libsys_resolver.


